20 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (A collage of six images labeled: \215Caterpillar\216 showing a camouflaged caterpillar on a plant stem, \215Chameleon\216 with a chameleon blending into green foliage, \215Gecko\216 on a tree bark, \215Lizard\216 on reddish-brown rock, \215Spider\216 in a wooden crevice with webbing, and \215Locust\216 in grassy terrain. Each creature is camouflaged in its natural environment.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Four-panel image showing various outdoor environments with red rectangles highlighting subjects of interest. Panel a: Green moss growing on a tree trunk. Panel b: A hummingbird hovering near red flowers. Panel c: Close-up of green leaves with small black spots marked. Panel d: Dry grass and sparse vegetation on sandy soil.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Process of image augmentation illustrated in three steps. A random image \(A\) shows plants with highlighted sections for object extraction. These objects are resized and rotated randomly. The transformation is applied to another random image \(B\), resulting in a synthetic augmented image with multiple highlighted sections.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Diagram of a deep learning model architecture. It shows an input image processed through ResNet50 with several convolutional and pooling layers, generating feature maps. Features are then integrated into a fine-grained score predictor and MaskMLP modules. The x6 Encoder and Decoder sections employ multi-scale deformable self-attention, cross-attention, feed-forward networks, and denoising mechanisms, leading to output boxes and classifications.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a neural network architecture involving ResNet50. Image features pass through ResNet50, producing feature maps \\\( F_i \\\). These are processed by MLPs, \\\( MLP_s \\\) and \\\( MLP_c \\\), which undergo linear and ReLU transformations. Outputs are combined using a sigmoid operation, affecting a grass image. Component details: MLP uses linear layers with dimensions \\\( 256 \\to 512 \\\) and \\\( 512 \\to 256 \\\), producing outputs \\\( W_s \\\) and \\\( W_c \\\).) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating object recognition in an image. The original image is divided into a grid with blue X's marking irrelevant regions and red dots indicating relevant regions. Lines connect these areas to a set of object queries below, distinguishing between matching \(red lines\) and non-matching queries \(blue lines\). A second section shows filtered object queries with retained relevance, connecting to an adjusted image grid. A key explains symbols: blue X for irrelevance, red dot for relevance, blue line for non-match, and red line for match.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
26 0 obj
<< /A 59 0 R /Alt (A set of two labeled image grids \(a\) and \(b\) each containing rows and columns. Each grid includes the \215Original Image,\216 \215Deformable DETR,\216 and \215Key-FG DETR \(Ours\)\216 for five samples. The images showcase enhancements using different detection models. \215Deformable DETR\216 and \215Key-FG DETR \(Ours\)\216 rows present heatmap visualizations highlighting targeted areas in the samples compared to the original images.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 47 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
27 0 obj
<< /A 60 0 R /Alt (Comparison of two image detection systems, Deformable DETR and an unnamed system, applied to images of grassy terrain. The results for layers Res3, Res4, and Res5 are shown as dark purple tiles with variations in color. Detection results include cases of successful detection of locusts with different confidence levels and one error detection.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 48 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
28 0 obj
<< /A 61 0 R /Alt (Top section displays three magnified, color-enhanced images labeled Res3, Res4, and Res5, each depicting different levels of data resolution. The bottom section shows a photo of green plants growing in soil. Red dashed lines connect areas in the larger image to corresponding sections in the zoomed-in images, illustrating data analysis or feature extraction.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 49 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
29 0 obj
<< /A 62 0 R /Alt (Two line graphs show the average precision \(AP\) over epochs for different experiments labeled EXP_A to EXP_E. Graph \(a\) displays data for 0-15 epochs, with low AP for EXP_A and EXP_B. Graph \(b\) covers 0-50 epochs, showing an increase in AP, especially for EXP_D and EXP_E. Each experiment is color-coded: EXP_A in blue, EXP_B in orange, EXP_C in purple, EXP_D in green, and EXP_E in red.) /K 1 /P 9 0 R /Pg 49 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
